cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "L8 myoblast bioprinting finite element and Gaussian process framework"
abstract: >-
  Axisymmetric finite element model (DOLFINx 0.10) of shear-thinning flow, with inertia,
  through the cartridge and nozzle of an extrusion bioprinter, coupled to the damage law of
  Ning and co-workers (2018) for L8 myoblasts, and a Gaussian process surrogate that maps applied
  pressure and nozzle diameter to flow rate, wall shear stress and predicted cell damage.
  The damage law includes a pressure-independent term fitted to the damage measured in that
  study. Includes the 32-case simulation grid, the surrogate validation and its comparison with interpolants, the FEM
  checks of the operating window, the comparisons with published data, the same pipeline
  for RSC96 Schwann cells and the scripts behind every figure of the accompanying article.
